.It Fl -async-mirror-keep Ns = Ns Ar guid
Resolves an async mirror with divergent child histories, such as when its
lagging child was imported alone and written while the leader held writes
that the lagging child did not receive.
Such an import is otherwise refused, and the error names the guid and the
newest transaction group of each copy.
The import keeps the copy of the child with this
.Ar guid ,
erases the uberblocks of the other child before it writes anything, and
resilvers that child in full from the kept copy.
All writes that only the other copy holds are lost.
Inspect each copy first with a read-only import of it alone.
The option has no effect on a read-only import, or when the copies were not
written separately.
The guid must be a positive number.
The option needs the name or guid of one pool, and cannot be used with
.Fl a .
See
.Xr zpoolconcepts 7
for the durability rules and pool layout limits.
.It Fl s
Scan using the default search path, the libblkid cache will not be
consulted.
A custom search path may be specified by setting the
.Sy ZPOOL_IMPORT_PATH
environment variable.
.It Fl X
Used with the
.Fl F
recovery option.
Determines whether extreme measures to find a valid txg should take place.
This allows the pool to
be rolled back to a txg which is no longer guaranteed to be consistent.
